<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//NLM//DTD Journal Archiving and Interchange DTD v2.3 20070202//EN" "archivearticle.dtd"><article xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" article-type="correction" xml:lang="EN"><?properties open_access?><front><journal-meta><journal-id journal-id-type="nlm-ta">Cell Microbiol</journal-id><journal-id journal-id-type="publisher-id">cmi</journal-id><journal-title>Cellular Microbiology</journal-title><issn pub-type="ppub">1462-5814</issn><issn pub-type="epub">1462-5822</issn><publisher><publisher-name>Blackwell Publishing Ltd</publisher-name></publisher></journal-meta><article-meta><article-id pub-id-type="pmc">2253700</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1462-5822.2007.00983.x</article-id><article-categories><subj-group subj-group-type="heading"><subject>Erratum</subject></subj-group></article-categories><title-group><article-title><italic>Plasmodium</italic> sporozoites trickle out of the injection site</article-title></title-group><contrib-group><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Yamauchi</surname><given-names>Lucy Megumi</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="au1">1</xref></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Coppi</surname><given-names>Alida</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="au1">1</xref></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Snounou</surname><given-names>Georges</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="au2">2</xref></contrib><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Sinnis</surname><given-names>Photini</given-names></name><xref ref-type="aff" rid="au1">1</xref><xref ref-type="corresp" rid="cor1">*</xref></contrib><aff id="au1"><label>1</label><institution>Department of Medical Parasitology, New York University School of Medicine</institution><addr-line>341 East 25th Street, New York, NY 10010, USA</addr-line></aff><aff id="au2"><label>2</label><institution>Parasitolgie Compar&#x000e9;e et Mod&#x000e8;le Exp&#x000e9;rimentaux, USM 0307, CNRS IFR101, Mus&#x000e9;um National d'Histoire Naturelle</institution><addr-line>CP52, 61 Rue Buffon, 75231 Paris Cedex 05, France</addr-line></aff></contrib-group><author-notes><corresp id="cor1"><sup>*</sup>For correspondence. E-mail <email>photini.sinnis@med.nyu.edu</email>; Tel. (+1) 212 263 6818; Fax (+1) 212 263 8116.</corresp></author-notes><pub-date pub-type="ppub"><month>8</month><year>2007</year></pub-date><pub-date pub-type="epub"><day>30</day><month>6</month><year>2007</year></pub-date><volume>9</volume><issue>8</issue><fpage>2093</fpage><lpage>2093</lpage><copyright-statement>&#x000a9; 2007 The Authors Journal compilation &#x000a9; 2007 Blackwell Publishing Ltd</copyright-statement><copyright-year>2007</copyright-year><related-article related-article-type="corrected-article" vol="9" page="1215" id="N0x1d0d240N0x2097de0" ext-link-type="pmc"/></article-meta></front><body><p>In the <italic>Introduction</italic> to our article, we supported a statement about the loss of infectivity of sporozoites following <italic>in vitro</italic> incubation with an inappropriate citation: Vanderberg, J.P. (1975) Development of infectivity by the <italic>Plasmodium berghei sporozoite</italic>. <italic>J Parasitol</italic><bold>61:</bold> 43&#x02013;50. The correct citation that should be quoted is Vanderberg, J.P. (1974). Studies on the motility of <italic>Plasmodium</italic> sporozoites. <italic>J Protozool</italic><bold>21:</bold> 527&#x02013;537.</p></body><back><ref-list><title>Reference</title><ref id="b1"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yamauchi</surname><given-names>LM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title><italic>Plasmodium</italic> sporozoites trickle out of the injection site</article-title><source>Cell Microbiol</source><year>2007</year><volume>9</volume><fpage>1215</fpage><lpage>1222</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17223931</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>